1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,800
[whimsical orchestral music]
A Brief History of Physics

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,500
Padua, 1610. Galileo turns his telescope to the night sky.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,800
A cat keeps watch on the rooftop.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Night after night, four moons circle Jupiter.
The heavens do not all turn around the Earth.

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,700
Jupiter ripens into an apple…

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,300
Woolsthorpe, 1666. An apple lets go of its branch…

7
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,800
[bonk]
It falls on Isaac Newton.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,700
Throw it fast enough, and it keeps falling around the Earth:
the fall of an apple and the orbit of the Moon are one law.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,500
The orbit winds into a coil. London, 1831: Michael Faraday.

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,800
[needle ticks]
A moving magnet makes a current: electromagnetic induction.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,800
[spark]
The cat on the shelf wakes up.

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,500
Paris, 1898. Marie Curie holds radium,
glowing with its own light.

13
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:41,400
Atoms that break apart: radioactivity.
One ray of light races away…

14
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,800
Bern, 1905. Young Albert Einstein chases a beam of light,
the cat at his heels.

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,600
Near light speed, space shrinks and bends.
Gravity bends it most of all: a black hole.

16
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,000
[whoosh]
Space folds into a box.

17
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,400
Oxford, 1935. Schrödinger's box: a radioactive atom,
a Geiger counter, a flask of poison, a cat.

18
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,000
Unobserved, the cat is alive and dead at once.
Reality splits into every possibility.

19
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,400
Erwin Schrödinger lifts the lid.
All the worlds collapse into one…

20
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,300
[the lid slams shut]

21
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,900
[muffled meow]
[a Geiger click]

22
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:06,800
A Brief History of Physics
